{"kind":"article","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Learn about how to set up your project with the new authentication flow changes.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/atprotokit\/0210authflowchange"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/0210AuthFlowChange"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ATProtoKit"}],"title":"Archived: 0.21 to 0.26 Authentication Flow Migration","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This article documents the migration from ATProtoKit 0.21 through 0.26 and is retained"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only as a historical reference. Its examples and declarations do not describe the current"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ATProtoKit API."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Archived","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With the release of 0.26.0 comes a new migration flow for ATProtoKit developers. This change is fairly small, but this article will still cover what to expect in order to clear any confusion."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Authentication Flow","anchor":"Authentication-Flow","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Previously, when you wanted to authenticate to an AT Protocol service, you used an initializer from "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", which contained the "},{"code":"handle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"password","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameters. Then, you would use ATProtocolConfiguration.authenticate(authenticationFactorToken:) and passed the instance to the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoKit","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"class","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let config = ATProtocolConfiguration(handle: example.bsky.social, password: hunter2)","","Task {","    do {","        \/\/ You can put it in here…","        try await config.authenticate()","","        let atProto = ATProtoKit(sessionConfiguration: config)","","        \/\/ Or here…","        try await config.authenticate()","    } catch {","        throw error","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With version 0.26, this has been changed slightly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let config = ATProtocolConfiguration()","","Task {","    do {","","        let atProto = ATProtoKit(sessionConfiguration: config)","","        \/\/ Enter the handle and password in here.","        try await config.authenticate(","            handle: example.bsky.social,","            password: hunter2","        )","    } catch {","        throw error","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are the changes being made:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration"},{"type":"text","text":"’s initializer no longer takes the "},{"code":"handle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"password","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameters: now, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration\/authenticate(with:password:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is responsible."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the only external change. However, more has been made internally:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/UserSession"},{"type":"text","text":" is no longer stored inside of "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration"},{"type":"text","text":": now, a new "},{"code":"actor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" named "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/UserSessionRegistry"},{"type":"text","text":" holds all instances of the "},{"code":"struct","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value has been added to the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"class","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This value is linked to all objects that are related to the session. This is part of the new initializer for "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration"},{"type":"text","text":", named "},{"code":"ATProtocolConfiguration.init(pdsURL:keychainProtocol:configuration:canResolve:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration"},{"type":"text","text":" now closely follows "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/SessionConfiguration"},{"type":"text","text":". In fact, the following methods are no longer stored in the "},{"code":"class","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but have moved to default implementations of the "},{"code":"protocol","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration\/authenticate(with:password:)","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ATProtocolConfiguration.getSession()"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration\/refreshSession()","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ATProtocolConfiguration.deleteSession()"}]}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"protocol"},{"type":"text","text":", named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SecureKeychainProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":", will now manage the management of the password, access token, and refresh token. An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actor"},{"type":"text","text":", named "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/AppleSecureKeychain","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is available for applications running on Apple’s platforms."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","text":"`SessionConfiguration`","anchor":"SessionConfiguration","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As mentioned previously, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/SessionConfiguration","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" now has default configurations for each of the required methods. It is also "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" and requires a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"class"},{"type":"text","text":" to conform to it. The default implementation assumes you’re using an App Password to authenticate by default, but you’re able to create new implementations for your own conforming "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"class"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Furthermore, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionConfiguration.authenticate(with:password:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method handles Two-Factor Authentication by waiting on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionConfiguration.codeStream"},{"type":"text","text":" after the server requests a code. Pass the code back through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionConfiguration.receiveCodeFromUser(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":". The same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":"-related properties, named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionConfiguration.codeContinuation"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionConfiguration.codeStream"},{"type":"text","text":", can also support custom OAuth flows."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Auto-managing the Keychain","anchor":"Auto-managing-the-Keychain","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As mentioned earlier, a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"protocol"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actor"},{"type":"text","text":" have been made: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SecureKeychainProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/AppleSecureKeychain","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" respectively. This manages the keychain items for the password and refresh token, as well as storing the access token in-memory."}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The access token is being stored in-memory due to how frequently the token expires."}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/AppleSecureKeychain","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SecureKeychainProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" and is the default object used for Apple platforms. It’s also the default object used when initializing with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". However, you’re free to create your own implementation if it doesn’t suit your needs."}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At this time, Linux and Windows developers will need to implement their own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actor"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"class"},{"type":"text","text":" to achieve the same effect. However, default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actor"},{"type":"text","text":"s for those platforms will be created at a later date."}]}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/UserSessionRegistry":{"role":"symbol","title":"UserSessionRegistry","url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/usersessionregistry","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UserSessionRegistry","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A registry that manages ","type":"text"},{"code":"UserSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances, keyed by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/UserSessionRegistry","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UserSessionRegistry","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/ATProtocolConfiguration":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ATProtocolConfiguration"}],"url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/atprotocolconfiguration","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Manages App Password authentication and session operations for an AT Protocol account.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ATProtocolConfiguration"}],"type":"topic","title":"ATProtocolConfiguration","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration"},"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit":{"type":"topic","title":"ATProtoKit","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"atprotokit_icon.png"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Develop and manage client and server-side applications for the AT Protocol and Bluesky."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit"},"atprotokit_icon.png":{"type":"image","identifier":"atprotokit_icon.png","alt":"A technology icon representing the ATProtoKit framework.","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/ATProtoKit\/atprotokit_icon.png","traits":["1x","light"]}]},"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/ATProtocolConfiguration/refreshSession()":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Refreshes the legacy access and refresh tokens."}],"title":"refreshSession()","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration\/refreshSession()","url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/atprotocolconfiguration\/refreshsession()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refreshSession","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/SessionConfiguration":{"role":"symbol","title":"SessionConfiguration","url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/sessionconfiguration","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SessionConfiguration"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defines the request-time requirements shared by all ATProtoKit session configurations."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/SessionConfiguration","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SessionConfiguration"}]},"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/AppleSecureKeychain":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stores opaque credential values in Apple Keychain."}],"url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/applesecurekeychain","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AppleSecureKeychain"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/AppleSecureKeychain","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"AppleSecureKeychain","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AppleSecureKeychain"}]},"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/UserSession":{"type":"topic","title":"UserSession","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/UserSession","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UserSession"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UserSession"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Represents an authenticated user session within the AT Protocol.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/usersession"},"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/ATProtocolConfiguration/authenticate(with:password:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Authenticates an account with its handle and App Password.","type":"text"}],"title":"authenticate(with:password:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration\/authenticate(with:password:)","url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/atprotocolconfiguration\/authenticate(with:password:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"authenticate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"with","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"password","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/ATProtoKit":{"url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/atprotokit","abstract":[{"text":"The base class that handles the main functionality of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ATProtoKit"},{"text":" API library.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ATProtoKit"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoKit","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ATProtoKit","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ATProtoKit"}]}}}